# Local environment for the Ops Copilot demo.
#
# `make provision` creates a real `.env` file from this template, asks for the
# Hugging Face token once, and stores it with owner-only permissions. The real
# `.env` is git-ignored and must never be committed.
#
# Format rules, because both Make and the shell read this file:
#   - one KEY=value per line
#   - no quotes, no spaces, and no '$' inside a value
#   - '#' starts a comment on its own line
#   - only the keys listed below are ever read
#
# The security control flags (OPS_DEMO_FICKLING, OPS_DEMO_OPA,
# OPS_DEMO_PROMPT_GUARD, OPS_DEMO_COSIGN, ...) deliberately do NOT belong here.
# The Makefile sets them so the strict demo profile cannot be relaxed by
# accident.

# Hugging Face token with read access to the gated Prompt Guard model.
# Accept the Llama 4 Community licence once at
# https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-Prompt-Guard-2-22M
# `make provision` stores the token here as an active line.
# HF_TOKEN=

# Bearer token for the optional local gateway (POST /chat).
# `make provision` generates a random value when this one is absent.
# OPS_DEMO_GATEWAY_TOKEN=

# HMAC key for the optional S5 approval tokens. When absent, the demo uses the
# sandbox signing key that the S1 scenario creates.
# OPS_DEMO_APPROVAL_KEY=

# Local port published by the gateway.
OPS_DEMO_GATEWAY_PORT=8080
